              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अभ्रम् — abhram — \"a bank of cloud; a cloud\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आकाशे कृष्णम् अभ्रम् अस्ति। ākāśe kṛṣṇam abhram asti. There is a dark cloud in the sky."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A neuter noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अभ्रम् (abhram) is the word MW gives for a cloud and cloudy weather; MW reports a reading of it as ab-bhra, \"water-bearer\"; MW compares Greek ombros and Latin imber, \"rain\" (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
